From: Lukas Drescher <lukas.drescher@cscs.ch>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 00:18:47 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 48/49] feat(harbor_agent): Claude Code adapter, the native
 release uploaded into the sandbox

ClaudeCodeNemoGym (custom_agents/claude_code_nemo_gym.py) runs Anthropic's Claude Code CLI inside the task
sandbox against the Gym model server, like OpenCodeNemoGym and PiNemoGym:

- install: the native release binary, gzipped on the node (rl-infra fetch-claude-code.sh writes
  <dir>/<version>/claude-<platform>.gz and the .gz's sha256), is uploaded and unpacked to
  /opt/claude-nemo-gym/claude; the binary's sha256 from the release manifest is checked again in the sandbox.
  Harbor's own install needs curl, Node.js, npm and internet in the image.
- model: Anthropic Messages to ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL = api_base without /v1 (every Gym model server serves
  /v1/messages, also under the capture prefix); every model tier and the sub-agent model resolve to the policy.
- capture: compaction, retries, the non-streaming fallback, sub-agents and web tools (denied), MCP, the task
  repository's settings/hooks/commands, prompt suggestions, background tasks, prompt caching and the
  attribution block are off; --system-prompt-snapshot on resends the first call's system prompt verbatim;
  request timeouts are at least the agent's time limit (stream replay sends nothing before generation ends).
- run: one recorded command (installed_compat), `claude --print --output-format=stream-json --verbose`,
  stdin from /dev/null, events to agent/claude-code.txt, session to agent/sessions; --max-turns for max_turns;
  no ATIF trajectory (the model server's capture holds the rollout).

failure_classes.claude_code_end_flags reads the stream-json events (replies by message id, synthetic API-error
messages skipped; terminal_reason prompt_too_long or a context-length result text) with the rules shared as
_context_end_flags; app.py uses it when the trial has claude-code.txt and no flags file. README: Claude Code in
"Agents inside the sandbox".

Behaviour of Claude Code 2.1.326 measured against a stub of the Gym endpoint (rl-infra
experiments/claude-code-probe), both profiles: only POST /v1/messages, no side calls, no connections outside
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL; one root, system prompt and tools identical on every call; tool results never rewritten;
no retry on 529; --max-turns ends with error_max_turns without another call; a 400 "prompt is too long" ends
the episode (terminal_reason prompt_too_long). Tool calls echo as Claude Code parsed them (Edit's
replace_all default filled in, a string timeout turned into a number), which breaks the lineage fingerprint
until the next patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
