+**Claude Code** (Anthropic's CLI, closed source; `ClaudeCodeNemoGym`): the native release binary, gzipped on the node
+(rl-infra's `fetch-claude-code.sh` writes `<dir>/<version>/claude-<platform>.gz` and a `.sha256` of the `.gz`), is
+uploaded into each sandbox and unpacked to `/opt/claude-nemo-gym/claude`; the image needs `gzip`, and the binary's
+sha256 from the release manifest is checked again there if `sha256sum` is present. Claude Code speaks Anthropic
+Messages: `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` is `api_base` without its `/v1`, and every Gym model server serves `/v1/messages`
+(also under the capture prefix). The run is `claude --print --output-format=stream-json --verbose` with the tools
+`Bash`, `Read`, `Edit`, `Write`, `Glob`, `Grep`; events go to `agent/claude-code.txt`, the session to
+`agent/sessions` (`CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`). For capture the adapter turns off compaction, retries, the non-streaming
+fallback, sub-agents and web tools (denied), MCP servers, the task repository's settings, hooks and commands,
+prompt suggestions, background tasks, prompt caching and the attribution block, and passes
+`--system-prompt-snapshot on` so the system prompt of the first call is resent verbatim; request timeouts are at
+least the agent's time limit (stream replay sends nothing before generation ends). Every model tier and the
+sub-agent model resolve to the policy, so a stray side call is still visible in the capture. Claude Code sends no
+sampling parameters: use `sampling_overrides`. `max_turns` is the CLI's own `--max-turns`; Claude Code exits 1
+after an error (`result` event with `is_error`); the failure classes read `agent/claude-code.txt`. Behaviour was
+measured with rl-infra's `experiments/claude-code-probe` for the pinned version: one chain per rollout, no calls
+besides `POST /v1/messages`, no rewritten tool results. Tool calls echo as Claude Code parsed them (schema
+defaults filled in, numbers given as strings converted), which the capture's fingerprint has to allow for.
+
+```yaml
+harbor_agent_name: null
+harbor_agent_import_path: "responses_api_agents.harbor_agent.custom_agents.claude_code_nemo_gym:ClaudeCodeNemoGym"
+harbor_model_base_url: http://127.0.0.1:8000        # the tunnel's sandbox end
+harbor_agent_kwargs:
+  version: 2.1.326
+  claude_archive_dir: /path/to/claude-code          # <dir>/<version>/claude-linux-x64.gz (+ .sha256)
+  claude_timeout_sec: 1740                          # below harbor_agent_max_timeout, so the verifier still runs
+  max_turns: 100
+  model_info:
+    max_input_tokens: ${policy.max_total_sequence_length}
+    max_output_tokens: ${policy.generation.max_new_tokens}
+```
+
+| Option | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `version` | `2.1.326` | Claude Code release. Flags and environment were probed against this release; another one needs `claude_sha256` and the probe again. |
+| `claude_archive_dir` | required | Directory with `<version>/claude-<platform>.gz` and its `.sha256` (fetch-claude-code.sh). The `.gz` is checked against the sidecar once per process. |
+| `claude_platform` | `linux-x64` | Release platform (`linux-x64`, `linux-arm64`, `-musl` variants). |
+| `claude_sha256` | built in for 2.1.326 | sha256 of the binary (the manifest's checksum), checked in the sandbox. |
+| `claude_timeout_sec` | none | Claude Code is ended with exit 124 after this, so its log and exit status are recorded before Harbor's agent timeout. |
+| `claude_workdir` | none | Absolute path Claude Code runs in (created if missing); unset = the image's working directory. |
+| `claude_profile` | `default` | `default`: Claude Code's own system prompt and tool schemas. `bare`: `--bare`, a minimal system prompt. |
+| `claude_tools` | `Bash,Read,Edit,Write,Glob,Grep` | Built-in tools offered (`--tools`). |
+| `claude_settings` | `{}` | Deep-merged last into the `--settings` JSON; `null` deletes a key. |
+| `claude_env` | `{}` | Deep-merged last into the CLI's environment; `null` deletes a variable. |
+| `claude_debug` | `false` | Debug log to `agent/sessions/debug.log`. |
+| `max_turns` | none | `--max-turns`. |
+| `model_info` | `{}` | `max_input_tokens` / `max_output_tokens`: `CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_CONTEXT_TOKENS` / `CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS`, and the context limit for failure classes. |
